                  <msItem>
                     <title>Comment. Thome Aquinatis in quartum Sententiarum</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">John Marshall was bp. of Llandaff 1478–1496.
                        He gave 2 and bequeathed 8 books to Merton College (v. Powicke, Medieval
                        books of Merton Coll., pp. 219, 222).</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Not certainly part of the Windsor gift in
                        1612.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate/>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_596">Windsor, Berkshire.
                        Royal collegiate chapel of St George</orgName><p>'Orate pro anima
                        reuerendi in Christo patris domini Iohannis Marschull nuper Landauensis
                        episcopi et canonici istius Collegii qui hunc librum dedit ad communem
                        vtilitatem hic studentium', c. 1500, on label covered by tale and affixed to
                        the front cover of the 17th-cent. Oxford binding. 'Constabat doctori
                        Marshall episcopo Landavensi quondam hic canoncio qui contulit hunc librum
                        Collegio de Wyndesore. Qui alienaverit anathema sit Amen (s. xvi, on flyleaf
                        at end).</p><p>No sign of original chain mark.</p></provenance>
               </history>
